@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}
<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<p>
    ManageGames runs on your own machine and keeps all data in a local SQLite database.
    Nothing is sent to third parties, and there is no analytics or tracking.
</p>
<p>The app only sets the cookies it needs to work:</p>
<ul>
    <li><code>ManageGames.Auth</code> keeps you signed in. It ends when you log out, usually when you close the browser, and after two hours without activity.</li>
    <li>An antiforgery cookie protects the forms against cross-site request forgery.</li>
    <li>A short-lived message cookie carries one-time notices, such as a failed login, to the next page.</li>
</ul>
<p>Passwords are stored only as salted hashes.</p>
